9. Pull Request

A Pull Request is a request to merge changes from one branch into another.

PR Process
Developer
   ↓
Feature Branch
   ↓
Commit
   ↓
Push
   ↓
Pull Request
   ↓
Code Review
   ↓
Approval
   ↓
Merge
10. Continuous Integration

Continuous Integration means developers frequently integrate their code
into a shared repository.

Automated checks are performed after changes.

CI Process
Code Push
   ↓
Build
   ↓
Test
   ↓
Result

If tests fail, developers fix the problem before merging/releasing.

11. Continuous Delivery

Continuous Delivery automatically prepares software for release.

The application remains in a deployable state.

12. Continuous Deployment

Continuous Deployment automatically deploys successfully tested changes.

Code
 ↓
Build
 ↓
Test
 ↓
Deploy
13. Automated Testing

Automated testing allows tests to run without manually checking every feature.

Unit Testing

Tests a small part of the program.

Integration Testing

Tests communication between components.

End-to-End Testing

Tests the complete user journey.

14. Docker

Docker is used for containerization.

It allows applications to run consistently across different environments.

Docker Architecture
Application
     ↓
Docker Image
     ↓
Container
     ↓
Host Operating System
15. Dockerfile

A Dockerfile contains instructions for creating an image.

Example:

FROM nginx:alpine

COPY src/index.html /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html

EXPOSE 80

16. DevOps Security

Security must be included throughout the development lifecycle.

Never commit:
Passwords
API keys
Database credentials
Private keys
Authentication tokens

Use environment variables and secret-management systems.

17. Development Best Practices
Write clean code.
Use meaningful names.
Keep functions small.
Write tests.
Use Git branches.
Write meaningful commit messages.
Perform code reviews.
Document important processes.
Automate repetitive tasks.
Protect secrets.
